Normalization → Process of organizing data to reduce redundancy and improve integrity.
Primary Key vs Foreign Key
Primary Key uniquely identifies records.
Foreign Key creates relationships between tables.
Constraints
Rules enforced on data.
Examples: PRIMARY KEY, FOREIGN KEY, NOT NULL, UNIQUE.
Surrogate Key
Artificial key with no business meaning.
Example: author_id.
Avoid Data Redundancy
Use normalization and separate related data into tables.
ER Diagram
Visual representation of entities and relationships.
Relationship Types
One-to-One
One-to-Many
Many-to-Many
AUTO_INCREMENT
Automatically generates sequential values.
Default Storage Engine in MySQL
InnoDB
Composite Key
Key formed by combining multiple columns.
